  "known_differences_and_limits": [
    "Reactivating the current single-selected item emits Activate only. Upstream rc-menu 1.5.0 also emits onDeselect for this repeat; native Deselect is reserved for removing a key from multiple selection.",
    "Native popup motion uses fade/reveal instead of scaling an arbitrary subtree; the pinned GPUI revision is unchanged. Motion tests verify interruption, geometry and settling, while screenshots disable motion.",
    "Virtual custom popup width measures a bounded sample and the active item and may grow when a wider row materializes. Reference DOM measures every row. Set MenuStyles.submenu_list.w(px(...)) for a stable explicit width.",
    "Full pixel errors and paired images remain available. Text/vector antialiasing and shadow rasterization are backend dependent; automated color/bounds checks do not establish identical arbitrary custom glyph rendering.",
    "Native Windows roles, properties and actions were exercised through UI Automation. Interactive screen-reader sessions and native macOS/Linux rendering/accessibility were not verified.",
    "Release timings are local CPU/layout observations. GPUI ancestor invalidation and global focus refresh are included where reported; ancestor/focus isolation and cross-machine latency are not claimed."
  ]
